---
const rungs = [
	{
		level: "Level 1",
		style: "Preserve details",
		note: "The default request.",
		state: "Over budget → escalate",
	},
	{
		level: "Level 2",
		style: "Bullets",
		note: "Keeps level 1's output budget, so a reasoning model does not answer nothing.",
		state: "Over budget → escalate",
	},
	{
		level: "Level 3",
		style: "Mechanical truncate",
		note: "Stored like any other level, tagged [lcm:truncated]. This is what guarantees convergence.",
		state: "Always accepted",
	},
];
---

<figure class="not-prose mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl @container">
  <div class="grid gap-6 @3xl:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] @3xl:gap-10">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      {
        rungs.map((rung) => (
          <div class="rounded-blume border border-border p-4">
            <p class="font-medium text-foreground text-sm">
              {rung.level}
              <span class="text-muted-foreground"> · {rung.style}</span>
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-muted-foreground text-xs">
              {rung.state}
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground text-sm leading-relaxed">
              {rung.note}
            </p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <div
      class="flex flex-col gap-5 rounded-blume border border-border bg-muted/30 p-4 @3xl:w-64"
    >
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-foreground text-xs">gate</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted-foreground text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A result is accepted only when it is strictly smaller than its input.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-foreground text-xs">rich tier</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted-foreground text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A node over its target keeps the thorough text beside the terse one.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-foreground text-xs">budget</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-muted-foreground text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The cap comes from the engine's arithmetic, not the model's own count,
          so a pass cannot pass itself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figcaption class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground text-sm">
    Three levels, in the order a pass tries them.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
